# Retired documentation - kept locally, not tracked
garbage/

# Runtime capture artifacts written into the repo root by the app itself.
# *.log above already covers session.log / retroterm_console.log; the transcript
# logger writes .txt for DecodedText format, which nothing else caught.
session.txt

# Standalone Console programs are NOT how this repo tests anything - xUnit only.
# Two of these ("test-tdv-basic.cs", "test-tdv-keys-comprehensive.cs") sat untracked
# in the root for nine months, referenced by no .csproj, printing values and asserting
# nothing, while the same behaviour was already covered by real tests in
# tests\RetroTerm.Tests\TDV\. They were bait for anyone grepping for TDV key tests.
# If a scratch program is ever genuinely needed, it does not live here.
/test-*.cs

# Outside conformance corpora. These belong to other projects and are NOT committed here:
# nothing from another codebase lives in this repository. Fetch them when you want to run
# them with tools\fetch-conformance-corpora.ps1; the tests skip themselves when absent.
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/xtermjs/
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/libvterm/
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/vt340test/
tests/RetroTerm.Tests/Conformance/vt340regis/

# Scaffold written by repo-standards\tools\apply-standards.ps1. Copy from it, then delete it.
README.template.md

# Instructions to the AI assistant working on this machine. Kept locally, not published.
CLAUDE.md
